+---
+governs:
+  - utils
+---
+
+# ADR-130 — Reject inverted bounds in clampNumber instead of swapping them
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`clampNumber` takes `min` and `max` from callers that compute them. A caller
+can pass them inverted, and the function has to do something with that input.
+
+## Decision
+
+It throws a `RangeError` that names both values.
+
+## Consequences
+
+A caller that can produce inverted bounds orders them before calling.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Swapping the bounds. It returns a value inside a range nobody asked for and
+hides the caller's bug, so it was rejected.
